course: dictionary
lesson: 10273
title: Topsoil: the living top layer
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Topsoil is the top layer of soil. It is usually dark, rich and full of nutrients, which are the substances plants need to grow. Plant roots push down into it to get food and water.
explain: Read the context: «Topsoil is the dark upper layer with the most humus and life; below it lie subsoil and then solid rock.» Dark and upper tell you where it is. Life tells you it is full of living things, such as worms and tiny creatures.
explain: Soil is built in layers, like a cake. «Dig a deep hole in a garden and you see layers: dark crumbly topsoil, paler subsoil under it, then broken rock, and at the bottom solid bedrock.» Topsoil is always the top layer, so you look for it first.
fact: Topsoil is the top layer of soil, usually dark and rich.
fact: Topsoil contains humus, which comes from rotting plants, as well as worms and other tiny living things.
fact: «Soil has layers called horizons: dark topsoil, paler subsoil below, and broken rock above the bedrock.»
fact: Wind and rain can wash topsoil away. This is called erosion, so farmers and gardeners protect it.
fact: Plants grow their roots in topsoil, which is why it matters so much for growing food.
exercise: «Topsoil is the dark upper layer with the most humus and life; below it lie subsoil and then solid rock.» Where is topsoil? | *On the top, above the subsoil | Under the solid rock | Floating in the air | Below the subsoil
exercise: Farmers protect topsoil because wind and rain can wash it away. What is this washing away called? | Subsoil | *Erosion | Bedrock | Humus
exercise: Find and copy one word that shows topsoil is full of living things. | *life | rock | layer | garden
test: Why do plants grow their roots in topsoil? | Because it is pale and dry | Because it is solid rock | *Because it is rich and full of nutrients | Because it has no living things
test: «Dig a deep hole in a garden and you see layers: dark crumbly topsoil, paler subsoil under it.» How does topsoil look compared with subsoil? | Paler | *Darker | Red and shiny | Grey and wet
exam: Which is the best meaning of topsoil? | A plant food sold in bags | *The top layer of soil, dark, rich and full of nutrients, where plants grow their roots | Solid rock at the bottom of a hole | Pale sand that blows away in the wind
